# negative seed.
#
# Scenario: a `Softmax` capability cell claims `class: pure` but its
# definitions reference a provider with the wrong axis shape (`axis` on a
# scalar cell that declared arity 1) and no numeric policy. A compiler that
# silently admits would mint a CellId for an ill-formed pure cell and later
# branch on an invented provider axis.
#
# expect: E-CELL-003 / E-CELL-004 - typed refusal at the emath-ir admission
# seam (identity mutation or arity bound), never silent admission of a
# wrong-axis provider under a pure class.
use std.kinds.capability

emath capability Softmax:
    class: pure
    version: 1.0.0
    migration: bump-and-note "axis smuggle attempt"
    inputs:
        x: Float64
    outputs:
        probability: Float64
    definitions:
        probability = softmax(x, axis = 2)
